hadiths[44]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16544","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: in the mosque, placing one of his feet upon the other."
"16545","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik ibn Anas, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, from his father, that his grandfather said to Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim, and he was of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Can you show me how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution, Abdullah ibn Zayd said: Yes, so he called for water for ablution, and poured upon his hands, and washed his hand twice, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his hands twice to the elbows, then wiped his head with his hands, bringing them forward and back, beginning with the front of his head, then going with them to his nape, then returning them until he returned to the place he began from, then washed his feet."
"16546","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Abbad ibn Tamim, he said: Abdullah ibn Zayd said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and prayed for rain and turned his cloak."
"16547","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"16548","He said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for rain and turned his cloak."
"16549","He said: He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that he heard Abbad ibn Tamim say: I heard Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Mazini say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to the prayer place and prayed for rain and turned his cloak when he faced the qiblah."
"16550","He said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to pray for rain, so he faced the qiblah and turned his cloak and recited aloud and prayed two rakahs."
"16551","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with the people to pray for rain, so he prayed with them two rakahs and recited aloud therein and turned his cloak and supplicated and faced the qiblah."
"16552","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped his head with his hands, bringing them forward and back, and began with the front of his head, then went with them to his nape, then returned them until he returned to the place he began from."
"16553","He said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, go out to pray for rain, so he turned his back to the people and faced the qiblah and turned his cloak and kept supplicating and prayed two rakahs and recited aloud."
"16554","He said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Habban ibn Wasi, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution one day and wipe his head with water other than the remainder of his hands."
"16555","He said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Zayd, he heard Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution and kept saying thus, rubbing."
"16556","He said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab and Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no ablution except in what you find wind or hear sound."
"16557","He said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Amr, from his father, that he heard Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari asked about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he called for water and washed his hands and rinsed his mouth and sniffed three times and washed his face three times and washed his hands twice twice and wiped his head; Uthman said: Malik wiped his head, bringing his hands forward and back with them, and washed his feet, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution."
"16558","He said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Jurjah informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reclining in the mosque on his back, placing one of his feet upon the other."
"16559","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah al-Ansari informed us, he said: My father, and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said: Khalid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim, and he had companionship, so it was said to him: Perform for us the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: So he called for a vessel and poured from it upon his hands three times and washed them, then he put in his hand and took it out, and rinsed his mouth and sniffed from one palm, and did that three times, and took it out, then washed his face, then put in his hand and took it out, and washed his hands to the elbows twice twice, then put in his hand and took it out, and wiped his head, bringing his hand forward and back, then washed his feet to the ankles, then he said: Thus was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16560","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Indeed Ibrahim made Makkah sacred and supplicated for it, and I made Madinah sacred as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred, and I supplicated for them in their mudd and their sa like what Ibrahim supplicated for Makkah."
"16561","He said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placing one of his feet upon the other."
"16562","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for rain, so he faced the qiblah and turned his cloak."
"16563","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle: He saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the mosque reclining, placing one of his feet upon the other."
"16564","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of a man finding something in prayer, it seeming to him that something had come from him, so he said: Let him not leave until he finds wind or hears sound."
"16565","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he heard Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to the prayer place and prayed for rain, so he faced the qiblah and turned his cloak and prayed two rakahs; Sufyan said: Turning the cloak is making the right the left and the left the right."
"16566","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan al-Mazini al-Ansari narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution; Sufyan said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, seventy-four years ago, and I asked him after that shortly, and Yahya was older than him; Sufyan said: I heard from him three hadiths: So he washed his hands twice and his face three times and wiped his head twice; my father said: I heard him from Sufyan three times saying: He washed his feet twice, and he once said: He wiped his head once, and he said twice: He wiped his head twice."
"16567","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise; I read to Abd al-Rahman: from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Mazini, he said:"
"16568","Abdullah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Abbad ibn Tamim al-Mazini, from his father or his uncle, that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution and wipe with water upon his feet."
"16569","He said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abbad ibn Tamim informed me that his uncle, and he was of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with the people to the prayer place to pray for rain for them, so he stood and supplicated standing, then turned toward the qiblah and turned his cloak, so they were given rain."
"16570","He said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, so I brought out water to him, so he performed ablution, and washed his face three times and his hands twice twice, and wiped his head, bringing it forward and back, and wiped his ears, and washed his feet."
"16571","He said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Habban ibn Wasi, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution and wipe his head with water other than the remainder of his hands."
"16572","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between these houses, meaning his houses, to my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and the pulpit is upon a canal of the canals of Paradise."
"16573","He said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Wasi narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim, his uncle, al-Mazini, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution at al-Juhfah, so he rinsed his mouth, then sniffed, then washed his face three times and washed his right hand three times, then wiped his head with water other than the remainder of his hands, then washed his feet until he cleaned them."
"16574","Sakan ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim al-Ansari, that he heard his uncle, and he was of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and prayed for rain, then turned toward the qiblah and turned his back to the people, supplicating, and turned his cloak and prayed two rakahs; Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Turning the cloak is until the year changes, so high prices become cheap."
"16575","He said: Mansur ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: What is between my pulpit and my house is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"16576","He said: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for rain, and upon him was a black khamisah of his, so he wanted to take its lower part and make it its upper, but it was heavy upon him, so he turned it upon him, the right upon the left and the left upon the right."
"16577","He said: Muammal narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his father, he said: It was said to Abdullah ibn Zayd on the day of al-Harrah: Come to Ibn Hanzalah, the people are pledging, he said: Upon what are they pledging him, they said: Upon death, he said: I will not pledge anyone upon that after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16578","He said: Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, then al-Mazini, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution twice twice."
"16579","He said: Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, then al-Mazini, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution twice twice."
"16580","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Mazini say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to the prayer place and prayed for rain and turned his cloak when he faced the qiblah; Ishaq said in his hadith: And he began with the prayer before the sermon, then faced the qiblah and supplicated."
"16581","He said: Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Misri narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn Yaqub al-Ansari, that Habban ibn Wasi al-Ansari narrated to him that he heard Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim al-Mazini mention that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution, so he rinsed his mouth, then sniffed, then washed his face three times and his right hand three times and the other three times, and wiped his head with water other than the remainder of his hand, and washed his feet until he cleaned them."
"16582","He said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out and faced the qiblah supplicating and turned his cloak, then prayed two rakahs, reciting aloud in them, he said:"
"16583","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, and Attab said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, he said: Habban ibn Wasi narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim al-Mazini, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution at al-Juhfah, then he mentioned the meaning of Hasan's hadith, except that he said: So he wiped his head with water of other than the remainder of his hand."
"16584","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim, he said: When Allah bestowed upon His Messenger on the day of Hunayn what He bestowed, he said: He distributed among the people, among those whose hearts are reconciled, and he did not distribute and did not give the Ansar anything, so it is as if they found it hard, as they did not get what the people got, so he addressed them and said: O company of the Ansar, did I not find you astray, so Allah guided you through me, and you were divided, so Allah united you through me, and poor, so Allah enriched you through me, he said: Whenever he said something, they said: Allah and His Messenger are more generous, he said: What prevents you from answering me, they said: Allah and His Messenger are more generous, he said: If you wished, you would have said: You came to us such and such, will you not be pleased that the people go with sheep and camels, and you go with the Messenger of Allah to your dwellings, were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man of the Ansar, if the people took a valley and a path, I would take the valley of the Ansar and their path, the Ansar are the inner garment and the people are the outer garment, and indeed you will meet after me selfishness, so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd."
"16585","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, he said: When it was the time of al-Harrah, one came to him and said: This is Ibn Hanzalah, and Affan once said: That is Ibn Hanzalah, pledging the people, he said: Upon what thing is he pledging them, he said: Upon death, he said: I will not pledge anyone upon this after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16586","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti al-Tahhan, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rinsed his mouth and sniffed from one palm."
"16587","He said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to the prayer place to pray for rain, and upon him was a black khamisah, so he took its lower part to make it its upper, but it was heavy upon him, so he turned it upon his shoulder."
